<p>Thousands of people marched through central London on March 28 in a demonstration organized by the Together Alliance to oppose the rise of the far right in Britain. London’s Metropolitan Police put the crowd at around 50,000, while organizers called it the largest anti-far-right march in British history.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/myQx9NZvHFQyAO1TEKJ87kyTVxWxWni5KfLCvgFYgf-Goc12A9i8Xt2vJSarIqmOox5n5N-YreloOeZ28O-iajjYWjzh20_UEZwSfIdWjuGlm12FOgPcjl3PivV4PJrmJQN-WzAZLsSgJiYmRkb1Q648xtyRAfvpqXzZaKteVRs_MZMmJQ' alt='A protester holding a placard takes part in a march against the far right, organised by the Together Alliance, in central London on March 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Broad coalition: Le Monde reported that hundreds of groups organized the Together Alliance event, highlighting the breadth of coordination behind the march.</li><li>Poll backdrop: Reuters coverage carried by Al Monitor and The Straits Times said many demonstrators singled out Reform UK as the party led opinion polls at the time.</li><li>Institutional backing: Reuters coverage cited by Al Monitor said trade unions and civil society groups backed the demonstration.</li><li>Recent scale: Al Monitor said the march appeared set to be one of the biggest demonstrations in the British capital in recent years.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Police official: Before the march began, a police official cited by Reuters said about 30,000 people were expected to take part, showing that authorities anticipated a major turnout. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/protesters-march-london-oppose-rise-political-right'>Al Monitor</a>)</li><li>Some demonstrators: The Guardian reported that some protesters said they joined the march because of anti-racism concerns and support for Palestine. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2026/mar/28/london-protest-march-together-alliance-against-the-far-right-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Paige Horsford: The Kent teacher said she joined after witnessing racist incidents at her school, connecting the national rally to everyday local experiences. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2026/mar/28/london-protest-march-together-alliance-against-the-far-right-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/28/hundreds-of-thousands-march-through-london-in-stand-against-the-far-right'>Thousands march through London in stand against the far right</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/protesters-march-london-oppose-rise-political-right'>Protesters march in London to oppose the rise of political right</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/protesters-march-in-london-to-oppose-the-rise-of-political-right'>UK protesters march in London to oppose the rise of political right</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/28/protesters-rally-in-london-to-counter-rise-of-british-far-right_6751902_4.html'>Protesters rally in London to counter rise of British far right</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2026/mar/28/london-protest-march-together-alliance-against-the-far-right-latest-news-updates'>‘The tide is turning’, Green party leader tells crowd at march against far right – live</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>